{"qid": "76265631", "kind": "insufficient_context", "language": "python", "title": "ChromaDb add single document, only if it doesn't exist", "answer": "You can use the `add_document` method of the `Chroma` class to add a single document to the vector store. This method will check if the document already exists in the vector store before adding it. If the document does not exist, it will get the embeddings for the document and add it to the vector store.\n\nHere is an example of how you can use this method:\n\n```python\nfrom langchain.vectorstores import Chroma\n\n# Initialize the Chroma vector store\ndb = Chroma.from_documents([], embeddings, persist_directory='db')\n\n# Add a single document to the vector store\ndb.add_document(page_content='This is a test document', metadata={'title': 'Test Document'})\n```\n\nThis will check if the document already exists in the vector store, and if it does not exist, it will get the embeddings for the document and add it to the vector store.\n\nIf you want to add a document that already exists, you can pass the `id` parameter to the `add_document` method. For example:\n\n```python\ndb.add_document(page_content='This is a test document', metadata={'title': 'Test Document'}, id='existing_document_id')\n```\n\nThis will add the document to the vector store without getting the embeddings for it again.\n\nIf you want to add multiple documents at once, you can pass a list of documents to the `add_documents` method. For example:\n\n```python\ndb.add_documents([{'page_content': 'This is a test document', 'metadata': {'title': 'Test Document'}}, {'page_content': 'This is another test document', 'metadata': {'title': 'Another Test Document'}}])\n```\n\nThis will add both documents to the vector store without getting the embeddings for them again.\n\nI hope this helps!\n", "valid_output": true, "insufficient_information": false, "retrieved": ["llama_index/docs/docs/understanding/storing/storing.md_0_4924", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/indexing.ipynb_0_7842", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/vectorstores.mdx_0_5549", "langchain/libs/partners/chroma/langchain_chroma/vectorstores.py_4107_13535", "langchainjs/docs/core_docs/docs/integrations/vectorstores/chroma.ipynb_0_6875", "langchain/docs/docs/integrations/vectorstores/chroma.ipynb_0_6483"], "n_candidates": 62, "cited_doc_ids": ["langchain/docs/docs/how_to/indexing.ipynb_0_7842", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/vectorstores.mdx_0_5549", "langchain/libs/partners/chroma/langchain_chroma/vectorstores.py_4107_13535", "langchainjs/docs/core_docs/docs/integrations/vectorstores/chroma.ipynb_0_6875", "langchain/docs/docs/integrations/vectorstores/chroma.ipynb_0_6483"], "invalid_citations": [], "repaired_citations": [["llama_index/docs/docs/how_to/indexing.ipynb_0_7842", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/indexing.ipynb_0_7842"]], "generation_s": 77.68043169999146, "prompt_tokens": 3450, "output_tokens": 528, "config": {"tokenizer": "word_stem", "top_k": 6, "max_chars": 2000, "max_tokens": 800, "prompt": "e988f60a3726", "answer_rules": 4, "assistant_llm": {"model": "llama3.2:3b", "digest": "a80c4f17acd55265feec403c7aef86be0c25983ab279d83f3bcd3abbcb5b8b72", "num_ctx": 8192, "temperature": 0.0, "seed": 42}, "context_version": 1, "sample": {"limit": 20, "seed": 42}}}
