{"qid": "77410975", "kind": "insufficient_context", "language": "python", "title": "How to use Langchain text splitter to reduce tokens in my text", "answer": "Langchain text splitter is used to split text into chunks of a specified size. In your case, you are using a chunk size of 1000 tokens, but this may not be sufficient for your 300-inch PDF. You can try increasing the chunk size to see if it helps. Additionally, you can use the `chunk_overlap` parameter to specify the overlap between chunks. A larger overlap may help to reduce the number of chunks and make it easier to input longer text into the prompt. For example, you can try using a chunk size of 2000 tokens with an overlap of 100 tokens. This will result in fewer chunks and may make it easier to input longer text into the prompt. ", "valid_output": true, "insufficient_information": false, "retrieved": ["langchain/docs/docs/tutorials/summarization.ipynb_14440_21723", "langchain/docs/docs/versions/migrating_chains/map_reduce_chain.ipynb_0_7362", "langchain/docs/docs/tutorials/summarization.ipynb_0_7359", "openai-cookbook/examples/data/example_pdfs/rag-deck.pdf_2245_11028", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/split_by_token.ipynb_7094_14506", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/summarize_map_reduce.ipynb_0_7085"], "n_candidates": 31, "cited_doc_ids": ["langchain/docs/docs/how_to/split_by_token.ipynb_7094_14506", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/summarize_map_reduce.ipynb_0_7085"], "invalid_citations": [], "repaired_citations": [["langchain/docs/docs/how_to/summarize_map_reduce.ipn", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/summarize_map_reduce.ipynb_0_7085"]], "generation_s": 52.65093070000876, "prompt_tokens": 3601, "output_tokens": 199, "config": {"tokenizer": "word_stem", "top_k": 6, "max_chars": 2000, "max_tokens": 800, "prompt": "e988f60a3726", "answer_rules": 4, "assistant_llm": {"model": "llama3.2:3b", "digest": "a80c4f17acd55265feec403c7aef86be0c25983ab279d83f3bcd3abbcb5b8b72", "num_ctx": 8192, "temperature": 0.0, "seed": 42}, "contex